    passageB2: `<p>New research has highlighted that even brief exposure to passive smoking, such as just thirty minutes, can cause temporary harm to a non-smoker's heart. While experts have been <strong>raising awareness</strong> about the health risks associated with breathing in other people's cigarette smoke for some time, public understanding of these dangers seems to be lagging behind.</p><p>In most countries, people are generally well-informed about the dangers of smoking itself. Whether or not they choose to quit, they are aware that smoking can <strong>lead to</strong> respiratory illnesses, including serious conditions like lung cancer. However, their understanding of the consequences of passive smoking appears to be much more limited. They may not realize the <strong>severity</strong> of the threat. </p><p>Many non-smokers view smoking as an <strong>inconsiderate</strong> habit that causes them discomfort, rather than recognizing it as a genuine health hazard. They might object to smoky environments, dirty ashtrays, or the litter caused by discarded cigarette ends. They may consistently choose non-smoking sections in restaurants or other public places. Yet, a large number of them still don't fully grasp that being around smokers can actually make them sick, which is a <strong>cause for concern</strong>.</p><p>It's been known for several years that passive smoking can, to a lesser degree, cause the same respiratory diseases that active smoking does. People with asthma often find that their symptoms <strong>worsen</strong> significantly in environments filled with cigarette smoke. This can <strong>trigger</strong> an attack.</p><p>Smokers who are concerned about their health can try to <strong>break free from</strong> their addiction, which is one of the most common forms of dependence. They might rely on their own willpower, or they might use nicotine patches as a <strong>tool</strong> to help them quit. However, non-smokers often have limited options other than avoiding the company of smokers, particularly those who <strong>chain-smoke</strong>. This may lead to <strong>social isolation</strong>.</p><p>If you want to minimize the risks of passive smoking, you can take some simple steps. Always avoid designated smoking areas in public places and <strong>enforce</strong> a no-smoking policy in your home. Furthermore, you can politely ask your friends not to smoke in your presence. You never know, they might even start to <strong>reconsider</strong> their own smoking habits, and this could <strong>prompt</strong> them to think about their health.</p><p>These small changes can <strong>contribute significantly</strong> to your overall health and well-being. Don't underestimate the <strong>cumulative effect</strong> of protecting yourself from secondhand smoke. It is <strong>paramount</strong> to prioritize your health.</p>`,
    translationB2: `<p>Yangi tadqiqotlar shuni ko'rsatdiki, hatto passiv chekishga qisqa vaqt, masalan, atigi o'ttiz daqiqa ta'sir qilish ham chekmaydigan odamning yuragiga vaqtinchalik zarar yetkazishi mumkin. Mutaxassislar anchadan beri boshqalarning sigaret tutunini nafas olish bilan bog'liq sog'liq uchun xavflar haqida <strong>xabardorlikni oshirib</strong> kelayotgan bo'lsa-da, bu xavflar haqidagi jamoatchilik tushunchasi ortda qolganga o'xshaydi.</p><p>Ko'pgina mamlakatlarda odamlar chekishning o'zi xavflari haqida yaxshi xabardor. Ular chekishni tashlashni tanlaydimi yoki yo'qmi, ular chekish nafas olish yo'llari kasalliklariga, shu jumladan o'pka saratoni kabi jiddiy kasalliklarga <strong>olib kelishi</strong> mumkinligini bilishadi. Biroq, ularning passiv chekish oqibatlari haqidagi tushunchasi ancha cheklangan ko'rinadi. Ular xavfning <strong>jiddiyligini</strong> anglamasligi mumkin.</p><p>Ko'p chekmaydiganlar chekishni haqiqiy sog'liq uchun xavf sifatida tan olishdan ko'ra, ularga noqulaylik tug'diradigan <strong>e'tiborsiz</strong> odat deb bilishadi. Ular tutunli muhitga, iflos kuldonlarga yoki tashlab yuborilgan sigaret qoldiqlaridan kelib chiqadigan axlatga e'tiroz bildirishlari mumkin. Ular doimiy ravishda restoranlar yoki boshqa jamoat joylarida chekilmaydigan joylarni tanlashlari mumkin. Shunga qaramay, ularning ko'pchiligi chekuvchilarning atrofida bo'lish ularni kasal qilishi mumkinligini to'liq anglamaydilar, bu esa <strong>xavotirga sabab bo'ladi</strong>.</p><p>Bir necha yildan beri ma'lumki, passiv chekish faol chekish kabi nafas olish yo'llari kasalliklarini kamroq darajada keltirib chiqarishi mumkin. Astma bilan kasallangan odamlar ko'pincha sigaret tutuni bilan to'ldirilgan muhitda ularning alomatlari sezilarli darajada <strong>kuchayganini</strong> aniqlaydilar. Bu xurujni <strong>qo'zg'atishi</strong> mumkin.</p><p>Sog'lig'i haqida qayg'uradigan chekuvchilar o'zlarining giyohvandlikdan <strong>qutulishga</strong> harakat qilishlari mumkin, bu esa qaramlikning eng keng tarqalgan shakllaridan biridir. Ular o'z irodasiga tayanishi yoki chekishni tashlashga yordam beradigan <strong>vosita</strong> sifatida nikotinli yamoqlardan foydalanishi mumkin. Biroq, chekmaydiganlar ko'pincha chekuvchilar, ayniqsa, <strong>tinimsiz chekadiganlar</strong> bilan birga bo'lishdan qochishdan boshqa imkoniyatga ega emaslar. Bu esa <strong>ijtimoiy izolyatsiyaga</strong> olib kelishi mumkin.</p><p>Agar siz passiv chekish xavfini kamaytirishni istasangiz, oddiy qadamlar qo'yishingiz mumkin. Jamoat joylarida chekish uchun ajratilgan joylardan doimo qoching va uyingizda chekishga yo'l qo'ymaslik siyosatini <strong>joriy qiling</strong>. Bundan tashqari, do'stlaringizdan sizning huzuringizda chekmaslikni iltimos qilishingiz mumkin. Bilmaysiz, ular hatto o'zlarining chekish odatlari haqida <strong>qayta o'ylab ko'rishlari</strong> mumkin va bu ularni sog'lig'i haqida o'ylashga <strong>undashi</strong> mumkin.</p><p>Bu kichik o'zgarishlar sizning umumiy sog'lig'ingiz va farovonligingizga <strong>sezilarli hissa qo'shishi</strong> mumkin. O'zingizni ikkilamchi tutundan himoya qilishning <strong>yig'indisi ta'sirini</strong> kam baholamang. Sog'lig'ingizni birinchi o'ringa qo'yish <strong>muhim</strong>.</p>`,
