    passageC1: `<p>Mounting evidence, culminating in recent studies, has revealed the insidious nature of passive smoking, demonstrating that even brief exposure, such as a mere thirty minutes, can <strong>precipitate transient cardiovascular compromise</strong> in non-smokers. While experts have long cautioned against the <strong>deleterious health effects</strong> stemming from involuntary inhalation of secondhand smoke, public awareness regarding the gravity of these risks remains, disconcertingly, <strong>suboptimal</strong>.</p>

<p>Despite widespread dissemination of information concerning the perils of active smoking, including its causal link to respiratory illnesses and life-threatening conditions like lung cancer, a significant disparity exists in the public's comprehension of the <strong>ramifications</strong> of passive smoking. Whether individuals choose to heed warnings about active smoking is a matter of personal agency; however, the <strong>pervasive lack of understanding</strong> regarding the dangers faced by those exposed to secondhand smoke represents a critical public health concern.</p>

<p>For many non-smokers, the primary objection to smoking <strong>centers on</strong> its perceived antisocial nature and the immediate discomfort it engenders – the offensive odour, the unsightly ashtrays, the ubiquitous litter of discarded cigarette ends. While they may <strong>assiduously</strong> seek out smoke-free zones in public spaces, a substantial number remain unaware that mere proximity to smokers can <strong>render them susceptible to</strong> tangible health detriments. The notion that secondhand smoke is simply an annoyance, rather than a genuine health hazard, <strong>continues to hold sway</strong>.</p>

<p>The scientific community has, for some time, acknowledged that passive smoking can, albeit to a lesser degree than active smoking, <strong>induce</strong> similar respiratory ailments. Individuals with pre-existing conditions, such as asthma, often experience a marked <strong>exacerbation</strong> of their symptoms in environments saturated with cigarette smoke. Indeed, the impact of secondhand smoke on respiratory health is now <strong>irrefutable</strong>.</p>

<p>Smokers who are genuinely concerned about their well-being may elect to <strong>break free from</strong> their nicotine addiction, a notoriously difficult undertaking. Their strategies might range from leveraging sheer willpower to employing nicotine replacement therapies, such as transdermal patches. Non-smokers, however, are largely limited to mitigating their exposure by avoiding smokers, particularly those who <strong>habitually chain-smoke</strong>. </p>

<p>To mitigate the risks associated with passive smoking, individuals can adopt simple, yet effective, preventative measures. These include consistently avoiding designated smoking areas in public settings, <strong>enforcing a strict no-smoking policy</strong> within one's own home, and, where appropriate, politely requesting that friends refrain from smoking in their presence. Such actions might, <strong>perchance</strong>, even <strong>prompt</strong> those friends to <strong>re-evaluate</strong> their own smoking habits and prioritize their health. It is a collective responsibility to foster environments free from the <strong>insidious threat</strong> of secondhand smoke.</p>`,
    translationC1: `<p>So‘nggi tadqiqotlar bilan yakunlangan tobora ortib borayotgan dalillar passiv chekishning yashirin xususiyatini ochib berdi va hatto qisqa vaqt, masalan, atigi o‘ttiz daqiqa ta’sir qilish ham chekmaydigan odamlarda <strong>vaqtinchalik yurak-qon tomir buzilishiga olib kelishi</strong> mumkinligini ko‘rsatmoqda. Mutaxassislar uzoq vaqtdan beri ikkilamchi tutunni beixtiyor nafas olishdan kelib chiqadigan <strong>salomatlik uchun zararli oqibatlar</strong> haqida ogohlantirgan bo'lsalar ham, bu xavflarning jiddiyligi to'g'risida jamoatchilik xabardorligi, afsuski, <strong>yetarli emas</strong>.</p>

<p>Faol chekishning xavflari, jumladan, uning nafas olish kasalliklari va o‘pka saratoni kabi hayot uchun xavfli kasalliklar bilan bog‘liqligi haqida keng tarqalgan ma’lumotlarga qaramay, passiv chekishning <strong>oqibatlari</strong> haqida jamoatchilikning tushunchasida sezilarli tafovut mavjud. Odamlar faol chekish haqidagi ogohlantirishlarga e'tibor berishni tanlashlari shaxsiy ixtiyoriy masaladir; ammo, ikkilamchi tutunga duchor bo'lganlar duch keladigan xavflar haqida <strong>keng tarqalgan tushunmovchilik</strong> jiddiy sog'liqni saqlash muammosini anglatadi.</p>

<p>Ko'pgina chekmaydiganlar uchun chekishga qarshi asosiy e'tiroz uning ijtimoiyga zid tabiati va u keltirib chiqaradigan bevosita noqulaylik - yoqimsiz hid, xunuk kuldonlar, tashlab yuborilgan sigaret qoldiqlarining hamma joyda bo'lishi bilan <strong>bog'liq</strong>. Ular jamoat joylarida sinchkovlik bilan chekilmaydigan joylarni qidirishlari mumkin bo'lsa-da, ko'pchilik chekuvchilarga yaqin bo'lish ularni sezilarli sog'liq uchun zararli oqibatlarga <strong>olib kelishi</strong> mumkinligini bilishmaydi. Ikkilamchi tutun haqiqiy sog'liq uchun xavf emas, balki shunchaki bezovtalik, degan tushuncha <strong>hali ham hukmronlik qilmoqda</strong>.</p>

<p>Ilmiy hamjamiyat bir muncha vaqtdan beri passiv chekish, faol chekishga qaraganda kamroq darajada bo'lsa ham, shunga o'xshash nafas olish kasalliklarini <strong>keltirib chiqarishi</strong> mumkinligini tan olgan. Astma kabi oldindan mavjud bo'lgan kasalliklari bo'lgan odamlar ko'pincha sigaret tutuni bilan to'yingan muhitda o'z alomatlarining sezilarli <strong>kuchayishini</strong> his qilishadi. Darhaqiqat, ikkilamchi tutunning nafas olish salomatligiga ta'siri endi <strong>inkor etib bo'lmaydi</strong>.</p>

<p>O'z farovonligi haqida chinakam qayg'uradigan chekuvchilar nikotin qaramligidan <strong>xalos bo'lishni</strong> tanlashlari mumkin, bu juda qiyin ish. Ularning strategiyalari oddiy iroda kuchidan tortib, transdermal yamoqlar kabi nikotin o'rnini bosuvchi terapiyalardan foydalanishgacha bo'lishi mumkin. Biroq, chekmaydiganlar asosan chekuvchilardan, ayniqsa, <strong>doimiy ravishda sigaret ketidan sigaret chekadiganlardan</strong> qochish orqali o'z ta'sirini kamaytirish bilan cheklanadi.</p>

<p>Passiv chekish bilan bog'liq xavflarni kamaytirish uchun odamlar oddiy, ammo samarali profilaktika choralarini ko'rishlari mumkin. Bularga jamoat joylarida chekish uchun ajratilgan joylardan doimiy ravishda qochish, o'z uylarida <strong>qattiq chekmaslik siyosatini amalga oshirish</strong> va, kerak bo'lganda, do'stlardan ularning huzurida chekmaslikni muloyimlik bilan so'rash kiradi. Bunday harakatlar, <strong>ehtimol</strong>, hatto o'sha do'stlarni o'zlarining chekish odatlarini <strong>qayta ko'rib chiqishga</strong> va o'z sog'liqlarini birinchi o'ringa qo'yishga <strong>undashi</strong> mumkin. Ikkilamchi tutunning <strong>yashirin xavfidan</strong> xoli muhitni yaratish - bu jamoaviy mas'uliyatdir.</p>`,
